❌ Mistake in Your Answer
You said:
receiver seq no == 11 then ack for this packet
⚠️ This is wrong.
Receiver will NOT ACK Seq = 11.
Why?
Because PCIe Data Link Layer requires in-order delivery.
If receiver is expecting Seq = 10 but gets Seq = 11:
→ It detects a sequence number mismatch
→ It does NOT pass Seq = 11 to TL
→ It does NOT ACK 11
________________________________________
✅ Correct Behaviour (Very Important)
At Receiver:
Expected sequence number = 10
Received = 11
👉 Sequence mismatch detected
Receiver will:
•	Discard Seq = 11
•	Send NAK indicating expected sequence number = 10
NAK contains:
“I am expecting sequence number 10”
________________________________________
✅ At Transmitter:
When NAK(10) is received:
•	Transmitter replays starting from sequence 10
•	It retransmits:
o	Seq 10
o	Seq 11
o	Seq 12… (if any)
⚠️ It replays ALL unacknowledged TLPs starting from NAK sequence number.
________________________________________
🔥 Important Rule
Receiver NEVER ACKs out-of-order TLPs.
This is strict rule in PCIe.
