✅ Now Important Part (You Missed This)
What does receiver do when it sees duplicate packets?
Receiver is expecting:
Expected Sequence Number = 203
But it receives:
•	200 (duplicate)
Sequence mismatch!
Now this is where PCIe is smart.
________________________________________
🧠 Receiver Behavior for Duplicate TLP
Receiver checks:
If received sequence number < expected sequence number
→ It is a duplicate replay packet
Receiver will:
•	Discard duplicate TLP
•	NOT deliver to TL (very important)
•	Send ACK again (cumulative ACK up to 202)
________________________________________
🚨 Very Important Rule
Duplicate replay packets NEVER reach Transaction Layer.
DLL filters them.
________________________________________
🔥 So Final Flow
Replay Timer expires →
Transmitter replays 200, 201, 202 →
Receiver detects duplicates →
Drops them →
Sends ACK(202) again →
Transmitter finally removes them from Replay Buffer
System continues normally.
